      "review": "A small ، is printed immediately to the right of يَا in يَا وَاسِعُ (likely a stray mark); kept as printed. يَا مَتِيْنُ is set in a different font and alone shows sukūn on the yā. The honorific on this page is a small جَلَّ جَلَالُهُ glyph, written ﷻ. Verifier: sukūn on the long ī/ū is in fact printed on every such name on this page (open jazm mark beside the ḍamma), not only مَتِيْنُ — added throughout; the ، before يَا وَاسِعُ is confirmed as printed."
